From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:23:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Add the AXP318W PMIC

The Cubie A7S is powered by an X-Powers AXP318W PMIC at address 0x36 on
S_TWI0. Its two switch outputs behind DCDC1 feed the board's 3.3 V
devices: SWOUT1 the Ethernet PHY, SWOUT2 the SD card, the eMMC, the I/O
bank PH and other 3.3 V I/O. Linux does not know about the PMIC, so no
device can name these rails as its supply.

Describe the PMIC with DCDC1 at 3.3 V and its two switch outputs. All
three are on when Linux starts, and they stay always-on: SWOUT2 also
feeds VCC-IO, and the SD card supply has no load switch, so it is never
cut. SWOUT1 also feeds bank PD through R251, bank PJ and the TWI2/TWI7
pull-ups on J11; bank PJ and the pull-ups name no supply.

Not covered: the other rails, which stay as the boot chain set them, and
the PMIC interrupt, which nothing uses yet. The node is still an
interrupt controller, as the binding asks.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the AXP318W probes at
0-0036 and registers its regulators, vcc-3v3-sys at 3.3 V. A minute
after boot the output enable registers 0x11 and 0x12 read 0x1f and 0x17.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts   | 35 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index ad82a4425039..cfbe67e74b9d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -102,6 +102,41 @@ &r_i2c0 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&r_i2c0_pl_pins>;
 	status = "okay";
+
+	axp318: pmic@36 {
+		compatible = "x-powers,axp318w";
+		reg = <0x36>;
+		interrupt-controller;
+		#interrupt-cells = <1>;
+
+		regulators {
+			reg_dcdc1: dcdc1 {
+				regulator-name = "vcc-3v3-sys";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
+			};
+
+			/*
+			 * Ethernet PHY, bank PD through R251, bank PJ, the
+			 * TWI2/TWI7 pull-ups on J11. Always on: bank PJ and the
+			 * pull-ups name no supply.
+			 */
+			reg_swout1: swout1 {
+				regulator-name = "vcc33-lcd";
+				regulator-always-on;
+			};
+
+			/*
+			 * VCC-IO (bank PB, console), SD card, eMMC, bank PH. Always
+			 * on: the card supply has no load switch and is never cut.
+			 */
+			reg_swout2: swout2 {
+				regulator-name = "vcc-io";
+				regulator-always-on;
+			};
+		};
+	};
 };
 
 &r_i2c1 {
